! mcp_bootstrap_p226.strap -- MCP printed page 226: the Input Program's
! end-of-job and tape-error tail (V EOJ4 .. V EE), lines 1-50.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.233, read at 400 dpi, 900 dpi for
! doubtful glyphs.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID CA000562  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 226"; the heading
! row's LOCATION field is 224607, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  50 lines, contiguous from 224607.40 to 224641.40 (a half
! word; next 224642.00), then blank paper.  Line 40 is a DDI at
! "000000.00+" and occupies nothing: line 39 is 224633.00 (a half-word
! B) and line 41 224633.40.  Remarks here are DECIMAL (-0569 then
! -0570), -0563 .. -0608.
!
! >>> LINE 40'S DDI IS NOT HANDED TO THE ASSEMBLER. <<<  It prints
!   40*  000000.00+  +00000017   BU,04 ,10   V D15   DDI(BU,4),15
! and strap_asm refuses DDI outright (printed p.180 line 25 is the
! precedent: carried as a comment, no !CHECK).  Line 47 references it
! on THIS page -- "/I,V D15,46" printing 740000.00 80: an immediate
! takes the DDI's 4-bit field (1111) LEFT-justified in the 24-bit
! address, C22-6531 printed p.30.  So that line 47 can assemble, the
! deck carries ONE stand-in, "VD15 SYN(BU,4), 15", the form printed
! p.179 used for Z RMTCC; with the DDI not handed over it is the only
! definition of VD15 in the merge.  It is NOT the printed card.
!
! GLYPHS.
!  * "V EOJ4" (line 6) prints a closed O; line 3's SVA,V U,V EOJ4
!    prints 224612.07 = line 6's location.  "V EOJ1" (line 8) prints
!    the round glyph open on the right (reads ECJ1); written O by the
!    word (End Of Job) and its sibling EOJ4.  Nothing on this page
!    references V EOJ1 -- rests on ink and sense.
!  * "V RBLC" (line 29): B, straight left stem at 900 dpi, not 8.
!    Nothing on this page references it.
!  * "V D15" (line 40) prints worn, reads C15; line 47's "V D15" is a
!    clear D.
!  * "V CWR" (line 46) and "D CCW" (line 42): the W is this drum's
!    narrow w glyph.
!  * Octal fields' open rounds ("C00000.62", "224610.CC") are 0.
!    Hex bytes: line 6 "C1", line 32 "C7", line 13/41 "C0", line 10
!    "C5" -- written 0 where the statement has no index to make C
!    (verified by assembly below); line 28 "C8" is CB- (C8 = CB+'s 48
!    with the minus bit), a true C.
!
! CARD SERIALS.  Right-hand serials ?A000562 .. ?A000607 (header
! CA000562; the prefix glyph has the straight left stem of D, as
! p.221 records).  Four pairs share a serial, the second line's remark
! printed in the LEFT remark column: lines 4/5 (565, -0566), 12/13
! (572, -0573), 23/24 (582, -0583), 41/42 (599, -0600).  Asterisks
! after the LOCATION on lines 1, 23, 46.

VT5     SYN, $9                      ! p.213 line 28 "V T5 SYN,$9" (landed)
VT2     SYN, $6                      ! p.213 line 29 (landed)
VT3     SYN, $7                      ! p.213 line 30 (landed)
VT4     SYN, $8                      ! p.213 line 31 (landed)
VU      SYN, $3                      ! p.213 line 25 (landed)
VP      SYN, $1                      ! p.213 line 26 (landed)
VH      SYN, 32                      ! p.213 line 7 "V H SYN,32", an INTEGER
VX      SYN, (8)0.0                  ! p.213 line 11 "V X SYN,0"
VX1     SYN, 0.32                    ! p.213 line 12 = VX.VH
VX2R    SYN, (8)2.0                  ! p.213 line 14 = VX2S.64 = 2.0
VCWR    SYN, 4.0                     ! p.213 line 15 = VX2R+2. = 4.0
VNX     SYN, (8)5.0                  ! p.213 line 16 = VCWR.64 = 5.0
VSU     SYN, 6.0                     ! p.213 line 18 = VID.VH = 6.0
VRCNT   SYN, 7.0                     ! p.213 line 20 = VRQB.VH = 7.0
VFCNT   SYN, 7.32                    ! p.213 line 21 = VRCNT.VH = 7.32
VTS     SYN, 8.32                    ! p.213 line 23 = VSTR.VH = 8.32; LV line 27 000010.62
VM1     SYN(BU,64), 262143.          ! p.213 line 9 "V M1 SYN(BU,64),262143."
DMCP    SYN, 32.0                    ! landed
DCCW    SYN, 2.0                     ! landed; p.102 line 11 "D CCW"
VNXT    SYN, (8)224456.40            ! landed decks (p.215 etc.), half word only
VACT    SYN, (8)224655.0             ! landed decks (p.215 etc.), half word only
VEE1    SYN, (8)224646.0             ! landed (p.215 BIT-EXACT); ,V EE1 line 44
VD15    SYN(BU,4), 15                ! STAND-IN for line 40's DDI -- see header

        SLC, (8)224607.40
